# samples/02-Validation – start it with: dotnet run --project samples/02-Validation
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5102

### 1. Constraints – all errors at once, in the application's error format
POST {{baseUrl}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "not-an-email", "phone": "123", "country": "FR" }

### …in Polish
POST {{baseUrl}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: pl

{ "name": "Jan", "email": "nope" }

### …valid: the normalized parameters, with the default country
POST {{baseUrl}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Jan Kowalski", "email": "jan@example.com", "phone": "+48123456789", "callAt": "09:30", "tags": ["vip"] }

### 2. Parameter validators – NIP checksum (C#) and IBAN (FluentValidation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nip": "526-000-12-47", "iban": "PL00 1234", "amount": 10 }

### …valid
POST {{baseUrl}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nip": "526-000-12-46", "iban": "PL61 1090 1014 0000 0712 1981 2874", "amount": 100 }

### 3. Rules (JsonLogic) – check-out before check-in, two guests in a single room
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roomType": "single", "guests": 2, "checkIn": "2030-11-05", "checkOut": "2030-11-01" }

### 4. Request validator (FluentValidation) – more than 14 nights
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roomType": "double", "guests": 2, "checkIn": "2030-11-01", "checkOut": "2030-11-30" }

### 4. Request validator (C#, with configuration) – the total is above maxTotal
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ANV-1", "quantity": 1000, "unitPrice": 49.9 }

### Unknown route – the error factory answers it too
GET {{baseUrl}}/nothing-here

### Broken JSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{ nope

### The registered validators (what the panel offers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/validators
